WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.710
Every episode of a show has an intro,
and nothing tells you where it is.

2
00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.006
I wanted a skip intro button
anyway, so Watch listens for it.

3
00:00:10.506 --> 00:00:13.808
It turns the audio into one
channel at eight kilohertz.

4
00:00:14.108 --> 00:00:15.619
Thirty-one times a second,

5
00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:19.281
it checks how the loudness shifts
between neighbouring pitches.

6
00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:23.375
Thirty-three bands, from the low
end of a voice to the top of it.

7
00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:28.509
Each moment becomes a thirty-two bit
hash, a tiny barcode of the sound.

8
00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:34.649
It's written in plain Node, because the
ffmpeg build had no fingerprint library.

9
00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:37.781
Now take two episodes
from the same season.

10
00:00:38.081 --> 00:00:40.868
Watch slides one barcode
strip past the other.

11
00:00:41.168 --> 00:00:45.109
Where the same theme song plays,
the hashes line up and light up.

12
00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:48.713
One match could be luck,
so other episodes vote.

13
00:00:49.013 --> 00:00:51.413
The stretch most of them
share is the intro.

14
00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:55.898
If only one episode agrees, it
gets flagged instead of trusted.

15
00:00:56.398 --> 00:00:59.590
Finally the edges snap to the
nearest cut in the picture.

16
00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.813
Skip intro lands right where the story
starts, with nobody marking a thing.
